    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2048" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">altĭtŏnans</span></b> ,
		antis, adj.
		alte-tonans, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>thundering from on high</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Juppiter,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Enn.
					Ann. 2, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pater altitonans,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Jupiter</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Carm. Div. 1, 12</span></i>
			.—Hence, in gen., of wind, <i>loud-roaring</i>: Volturnus, * <i><span class="en">Lucr. 5,
			745</span></i>.</div>
